WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:07.068
A private dashboard becomes valuable by combining selected inputs around a common operational purpose.

00:00:07.068 --> 00:00:12.311
CCTV events may provide motion, object, tamper, or camera-health signals.

00:00:12.311 --> 00:00:22.571
Local vision AI can add descriptions or classifications, but its output should be treated as an imperfect observation that requires context.

00:00:22.571 --> 00:00:28.726
Endpoint tools may report malware, suspicious processes, policy violations, or device isolation.

00:00:28.726 --> 00:00:36.250
Firewalls and network monitoring can contribute denied connections, unusual traffic, new devices, and service changes.

00:00:36.250 --> 00:00:42.861
Authentication systems can show failed logins, new sessions, privilege changes, and account lockouts.

00:00:42.861 --> 00:00:47.193
Vulnerability findings and asset inventory add exposure context.

00:00:47.193 --> 00:00:56.996
An alert involving an internet-facing, unpatched asset may deserve different priority than the same event on an isolated test system.

00:00:56.996 --> 00:01:05.888
Inventory data should identify ownership, business purpose, location, and criticality without becoming an uncontrolled repository of sensitive details.

00:01:05.888 --> 00:01:12.955
Environmental sensors can report temperature, water, smoke, power, enclosure state, or other safety-relevant conditions.

00:01:12.955 --> 00:01:18.655
Manual notes and incident records capture observations that automated tools cannot.

00:01:18.655 --> 00:01:24.354
They also preserve the reasoning behind escalation, closure, and tuning decisions.

00:01:24.354 --> 00:01:30.966
Each source needs an owner, collection method, expected update interval, and failure indicator.

00:01:30.966 --> 00:01:35.754
The dashboard should distinguish no events from no data.

00:01:35.754 --> 00:01:43.277
A quiet sensor may be normal; a disconnected collector may create a dangerous blind spot.

00:01:43.277 --> 00:01:44.873
Collect purposefully.

00:01:44.873 --> 00:01:50.117
Do not ingest every available field simply because it exists.

00:01:50.117 --> 00:01:56.272
Prefer the minimum data needed for detection, review, accountability, and legitimate operations.

00:01:56.272 --> 00:02:04.708
Document source reliability, time synchronization, retention, and access restrictions so combined data remains understandable and responsibly handled.
